abstract: >-
  Proposed, untagged v0.3.9-referee-revision candidate of the A001 paper
  package. The project-level concept DOI 10.5281/zenodo.21474351 identifies
  the continuing project record, not this candidate; no version DOI exists
  for this untagged revision. For the
  canonical real dual transport operator H=-i X_1 associated with the
  explicit Keller map announced by Alpöge, with Fable credited in the
  announcement for work leading to the map, the paper gives Hilbert deficiency
  indices n_+=n_-=aleph0. The revised main proof constructs the minus-i
  family from a forward maximal sheet and obtains the plus-i family through
  the measure-preserving sign involution. The synchronized Lean publication
  freeze is 2e40c4cab86a1ef97cb3334497d10081dfe33867; it is untagged and
  unreleased. It is a provenance-only successor to fbcdd034; theorem and
  audit source are unchanged. The historical theorem-source root is
  ff50f4a2a312591c2e5b26e71eb390ade9164b34. PUBLICATION_PROVENANCE.md records
  focused TheoremFPlusITransport (8,684 jobs) and
  TheoremFExtensionMultiplicity (8,692 jobs) builds, the full 8,702-job Lean
  build, and a nine-declaration axiom audit. Lean/build and math.FA/math.AG
  gates pass, as do the non-claims and package/metadata reviews. Dan approved
  publication on 2026-07-30; no tag, release, version DOI, or arXiv submission
  is asserted yet.
  Lean proves the exact aleph0 Hilbert-basis
  indices, the bounded canonical-core Theorems E-F, a bijective von Neumann
  classification for the specific H_X1_min, and an injective family of
  distinct self-adjoint-extension witnesses parameterized by unitary complex
  phases. The continuum lower-family corollary additionally uses the classical
  cardinality of the complex unit circle; that cardinal identification is not
  one of the cited Lean declarations. The paper does not identify the exact
  cardinality of the full extension type. No preferred extension,
  arbitrary-operator theorem, exact Hamel rank, strong CCR, physical selection,
  or rank-three Dixmier counterexample is claimed. The backward
  wall is retained as independent paper geometry and is not used in the main
  deficiency proof. Prior withdrawn claims remain documented in the erratum.
